<font class="pn-title">Charter</font><br /><br /><font class="pn-normal">(1230 total words in this text)</font><br /><font class="pn-normal">(15 Reads)</font> &nbsp;&nbsp;<a class="pn-normal" href="modules.php?op=modload&amp;name=Sections&amp;file=index&amp;req=printpage&amp;artid=1"><img src="modules/Sections/images/print.gif" border="0" Alt="Printer friendly page"></a></font><br /><br /><font class="pn-normal"><FONT SIZE=3>
<H1><CENTER>Guild Charter</CENTER></H1>
<H2>Our Mission</H2>
<P>Our purpose is to foster a community where having a good time is more important
than the acquisition of items, wealth or power. To that end, we hold our
mission to be first and foremost the amusement of ourselves and our companions
be they guildmates or merely friends. Second only to that is helping those in
need, be they guildmates or other. Having a good time should not (where
possible) be at the expense of others unless you know the person in question to
be of a good natured sort who can stand a good ribbing now and again, or of
such a foul temper that you feel no amount of restraint or kindness would make
any difference in their outlook. In which case, put your best foot forward, and
tease them as tactfully and mercilessly as you can. </P>

<H2>Guidelines and Beliefs</H2>
<P>Part of the purpose of this guild is to help one another in this wonderful
world of Norrath. As much as we would like to help in every situation sometimes
a problem is best handled by someone else. Below are some guidelines to things
we most definitely will, or most definitely will not help with. </P>

<P><B>Guildwars:</B> The Revellers will never be involved in a guild war. Period.
</P>

<P><B>Killstealing:</B> It is a fact of life that at some
point or another, you will have your prey stolen out from under you. You can
pretty much guarantee that sometimes, you will unwittingly steal from another.
Honest mistakes happen all the time and a little patience and understanding go
a long way. That being said, if someone is deliberately KSing you, please use /
petition and/or /report and let Verant deal with them.</P>

<P><B>Powerleveling and Twinking: </B> Although there are
many strong beliefs about both of these practices, we believe it is a personal
choice that each player makes in the developement of their character. That
being said, please do not ask on guild chat, or ever expect any other member of
The Revellers to power level or twink you. This is not the purpose of the
Revellers and no one in the guild owes any other members any items or exp by
divine right. If someone is nice enough to help you, thank them graciously. </P>

<P><B>Corpse Retrieval: </B> Sometimes, you die in a very
bad spot. It may be difficult or nearly impossible to get to your body without
assistance. In such a case please ask on guild chat for assistance with the
corpse retrieval of your body or of those of your companions. </P>

<P><B>Quest Items and Armor and Equipment (Camping): </B>
An important part of a character's progression is the acquisition of new items
and equipment raise one's level of effectiveness. Although it is wholly
appropriate to ask for assistance or company on a camp or quest, it is not
appropriate for you to ask someone to camp or quest for you. Especially if the
item you're trying to get is far beyond what is possible for your character to
attain normally. (For example, don't ask for assistance with completing your
class quest armor or camping an SMR at lvl 5).
<BR>
<BR>
<FONT SIZE=2><B>NOTE: <I>Although it is appropriate for you to ask for assistance, no one is required to assist you
simply by virtue of your guild status or your lvl. A proven dedication to your
guild and you character and a reputation for being friendly, helpful and
gracious are all factors in the possibility of assistance on a guild level. All
requests will be dealt with on an individual basis.</I></B></FONT></P>

<P><B>Sale of items through the Guild: </B> A person's personal property is their own to do
with as they wish. The Revellers do not make any claim to your items, nor
require any person to offer items to the guild first at discounted rates. That
being said, if you can afford to do so please contribute items to the guild
whenever you can. If you can afford to sell them at a discount, that's
wonderful. If you are affluent enough to be able to bestow it to someone, that'
s great too! Your generosity has a way of getting back to you in unexpected
ways and your guild leaders will take note of your past history of generosity
when the time comes that you may need something from the guild.
<BR>
<BR>
<FONT SIZE=2><B>NOTE: <I>Anyone caught buying or accepting guild items on discount or for free for the
express purpose of reselling such items outside of the guild at a profit will
be removed from the guild. Taking advantage of the kindness of others will not
be tolerated.</B></I></FONT></P>

<P><B>Planes and Dragon Raids: </B> The Revellers are
a community, not an army. At this time, it is unlikely that we will be
organizing any planes or dragon activities. It is entirely possible that we may
be invited to join other guilds on planes and dragon raids, but we will not be
organizing any at this time. </P>

<P><B>The Offer of Services to the Guild: </B> Many characters have unique abilities (Resurrection, Teleportation, Trade
skills (Smithing and Jeweling!), Commonly begged Buffs (SoW, Clarity, Invis),
or class abilities (Corpse Location, Tracking). These unique qualities are
valuable to the community and it would be appreciated if these were shared with
the guild when possible. That being said, these abilities belong to the
characters who have earned them, often cost them mana, time and attention that
could be spent elsewhere. So be courteous and respectful and remember that no
member of the Revellers owes you a Teleport, Rez, Buff or use of their trade
skill at cost. </P>

<P><B>Honor and Respect: </B> As a player without a
guild you are responsible only to yourself. If you choose to join The Revellers,
then you take on the additional responsibility of defending the honor and
building the respect of the guild. We don't expect you to become selfless and
dedicate all your time to others, or spineless or to change your fundamental
personality. Where possible however, if someone asks for help and you are able,
please assist them. </P>

<P>If there is a misunderstanding, even if you are in
the right, please keep a level head and try to negotiate towards a solution. If
someone is being unreasonable, do not sink to their level. If you cannot come
to an understanding, either remove yourself from the situation or use /petition
to ask for assistance. Civility and common courtesy are sorely lacking in many
situations in EverQuest. Part of our mission is to promote and display a more
respectful, cooperative attitude and atmosphere in Norrath, be that while you
are hunting, questing, camping, or during guild events. </P>

<P>Keep in mind
that all of your individual actions reflect on the guild as a whole. We
understand that there are difficult people and difficult situations that can
occur on a daily basis. Please try to keep cool about it and feel free to ask
for suggestions on how to handle such situations on guildchat. Many tense
situations can be defused when dealt with in a calm, cool manner. If you feel
they can't (and it does happen), don't resort to threats, insults, or vengeful
behaviour. Remove yourself from the situation or, if it's warranted, /petition
or /report. Verant is far better equipped to weed out the truly bad folks than
you, or The Revellers, are. </P>

<P><B><I>Please do not ever conspire to get
someone killed, either through intentional 'training', misinformation, or bug
exploitation.</B></I></P>

<FONT SIZE=2><P><B>NOTE: <I>If someone intentionally bites off more than they can
chew, and then yells their bloody head off expecting you to join in, you are
certainly under no obligation to assist them. By the same token, if someone
intentionally bites off more than they can chew because you TOLD them you would
help, they have every right to expect your assistance.</I></B></P></FONT>

<P><B>Please do not ever conspire to cheat or defraud another player of items or money.</P> </B>

<P>Original charter by  Kadzer Troublemaker.<BR>
Updated by Malken Gneebiter</P>


</FONT></font></td></tr><tr><td align="center"> &nbsp;&nbsp; <br /><br />[ <a class="pn-normal" href="modules.php?op=modload&amp;name=Sections&amp;file=index&amp;req=listarticles&amp;secid=2">Back to Guild Documents</a> | <a class="pn-normal" href="modules.php?op=modload&amp;name=Sections&amp;file=index&amp;listsections">Sections index</a> ]</td></tr></table></td></tr></table><br />
